#X obj 60 578 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 606 1 float: note number. Velocity is taken from inlet 2 \;   and velocity 0 is a note off. \; 1 list: note \, velocity and \, if you like \, the MIDI channel. \; 1 anything: a message \, see Messages. \; 2 float: velocity for the next note \, 0 to 127 (default 100). \; 3 float or list: raw MIDI bytes \, as midiin gives them. \; 3 anything: a message \, the same set as inlet 1., f 64;
#X obj 60 732 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 760 1 signal: left output. \; 2 signal: right output. \; 3 anything: info \, name \, 0-127 and value text for every \;   change \, the tones that play \, their names \, the channels. \; 3 float: SysEx bytes for midiout., f 64;
#X obj 60 854 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 882 name v: set a control \, in the values the CZ shows. \; name: report it as info. \; n name v: set it from a pot or a MIDI CC \, 0 to 127. \; ninfo name: report it as info. \; preset n: a factory tone \, read only. \; user n: a slot of the user bank \, 0 to 63. \; init: a plain sawtooth tone to start from. \; reload: the same tone again \, edits dropped. \; compare 0/1: hear the stored tone instead of the edit. \; store n: the edited tone into user slot n \, in memory. \; name text: rename the edited tone (16 characters). \; copyline 1 2: line 1 into line 2 (or 2 1). \; copyenv 1 DCW 2 DCW: one envelope into another. \; userwrite: write the user bank to cz4user-bank.syx. \; userread: read it again. Both also take a file name. \; usersend: the user bank as SysEx on outlet 3. \; presets \, users: list the names. \; op n: recall operation slot n \, opstore n: store it \, \;   opinit: back to one tone \, opwrite \, opread: the file \;   cz4user-op.syx \, ops: the used slots. \; bend f: pitch wheel \, -1 to 1 \, times bend. \; mod f: modulation wheel \, 0 to 1: vibrato. \; at f: aftertouch \, 0 to 1. \; sustain 0/1: hold pedal. \; channel n: MIDI receive channel \, 0 is all. \; txchannel n: channel of the controller feedback and of \;   SysEx \, 1 to 16. \; status: report tones \, operation slot \, channels \, voices. \; stop: all notes off (they release). \; reset: silence at once., f 64;
#X obj 60 1376 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MIDI 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1404 midiin: raw bytes into inlet 3. cz4~ takes notes with \;   velocity \, bend \, aftertouch \, program change \, CC 1 \;   (vibrato) \, 7 (volume) \, 64 (hold) and CZ SysEx. \; midiout: the floats of outlet 3 \, SysEx tones and dumps. \; cz4cc 1: the CC pages from 20 on \, on channel 1. \; Without midiin: send note lists and bend \, mod \, at \, sustain., f 64;
#X obj 60 1514 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1542 dcw (0): brighter or darker: added to the DCW of both lines. \; attack (0): faster (-) or slower (+) steps up to the sustain point of every envelope. \; release (0): faster (-) or slower (+) steps after the sustain point. \; balance (0): line 1 (-) against line 2 (+). \; detune (0): line 2 against line 1 \, in cents \, on top of the tone. \; vibrato (0): extra vibrato depth \, as the mod wheel. \; chorus (64): level of the chorus for tones with chorus on. \; volume (100): master volume., f 64;
#X obj 60 1732 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controller\ layer\ and\ editor 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1760 cz4cc is the controller layer: MIDI CC from 20 on in pages of 8 \, the same pages as for pdoly8~ \, tx81z~ \, d50~ and juno~. Page 1 is PERFORM \, page k is row k of the editor. It turns a CC into an n message and sends every change made elsewhere back to the controller as CC \, also when the selected line or envelope changes. Its argument is the MIDI channel \, and it follows the channels cz4~ reports. \; cz4edit is the editor: click it in the object area above. All 77 controls in rows of 8 \, the factory and user tones \, the operation memory \, the MIDI channels and the CZ handshake. It explains itself in its readme. \; All names are listed at the end of this patch with their CC numbers., f 64;
#X obj 60 1982 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty The\ instrument 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2010 A tone is a CZ tone: two lines \, each with a wave pair and a window \, and three envelopes per line with 8 steps each: DCO (pitch) \, DCW (the phase distortion \, which does what a filter does on other synthesizers) and DCA (amplitude). Line select plays line 1 \, line 2 \, line 1 twice with line 2 detuned (1+1') or both (1+2'). Line 2 can be ring-modulated by line 1 or have its pitch thrown about by noise. \; Every voice has its own six envelopes: the instrument is fully polyphonic. As on the CZ there are 8 lines: 8 notes of a one-line tone \, 4 of a two-line tone (voices raises this up to 16). \; From the CZ-1: 144-byte tones with line levels and velocity on each envelope \, names \, the operation memory with split and tone mix of two tones \, portamento \, glide \, bend range \, wheel and aftertouch \, and the chorus. The waves are those of the uPD933 chip as MAME models it \, computed with the chip's 12-bit tables (chip 0 gives ideal ones). \; From Arturia's CZ V the idea of simpler access: the PERFORM row changes brightness \, attack \, release \, balance and detune of the playing tone without touching it \, and the easy envelope writes a whole 8-step envelope from four values. Everything stays a CZ tone \, so it can go to a CZ and back. \; Timings the chip does not fix (vibrato clock \, velocity and key follow curves \, portamento \, glide \, chorus) are estimates for now., f 64;
