#X obj 60 5586 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Playing 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 5638 s \$0-cz4;
#X floatatom 60 5614 6 -1 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 5638 bend \$1;
#X floatatom 160 5614 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 5638 mod \$1;
#X floatatom 260 5614 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 260 5638 at \$1;
#X floatatom 360 5614 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 360 5638 sustain \$1;
#X text 82 5668 bend (0): pitch wheel \, -1 to 1. The range in semitones is the control bendrange. \; mod (0): modulation wheel \, 0 to 1. Adds vibrato \, as deep as wheel says. \; at (0): aftertouch \, 0 to 1: vibrato (atvib) and level (atamp). \; sustain (0): hold pedal. Notes released while it is 1 sound until it returns to 0., f 64;
#X obj 60 5794 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Selection 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 5846 s \$0-cz4;
#X floatatom 60 5822 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 5846 line \$1;
#X floatatom 160 5822 6 0 2 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 5846 env \$1;
#X floatatom 260 5822 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 260 5846 edit \$1;
#X obj 460 5876 s \$0-cz4;
#X msg 60 5876 copyline 1 2;
#X msg 190 5876 copyenv 1 DCW 2 DCW;
#X msg 320 5876 compare 1;
#X msg 60 5910 compare 0;
#X text 82 5944 line (0 = line 1) \, env (2 = DCA) \, edit (0 = tone A): what the line \, envelope \, rate and level controls work on. Changing them reports the values of the new selection \, the controller follows. \; copyline and copyenv copy within the edited tone \, compare plays the stored tone while it is 1., f 64;
#X obj 60 6054 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty SysEx 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 6082 The object speaks the exclusive format of the CZ series. A tone travels as nibbles \, the low one first: 256 for the 128 bytes of a CZ-101 \, 1000 \, 3000 or 5000 \, 288 for the 144 bytes of a CZ-1. The bytes arrive with the rest of the MIDI at the third inlet and leave the third outlet as floats. \; As a device it answers like a CZ \, with Casio's handshake: a send request (F0 44 00 00 7n 10 or 11 \, program) and a receive request (20 or 21) are answered with F0 44 00 00 7n 30 \, and the tone follows. So CZ editors and librarians work with it. Program 96 (hex 60) is the tone A that plays \, 32 to 95 the user slots 0 to 63 \, 0 to 31 the first factory tones. \; As a host it talks to a real CZ: czget p asks it for program p \, czsend p sends it the edited tone. czmodel 101 makes both use the 128-byte format of the CZ-101 family \, czmodel 1 (default) the CZ-1's. \; sysexdump sends the edited tone and usersend the 64 tones of the user bank as librarian messages (receive request with the data in the same message). Such messages and .syx files of librarians are taken at the third inlet or with sysex b b b., f 64;
#X obj 60 6400 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Data\ files 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 6428 The object needs no files. Without them the factory bank holds the INIT tone. \; Every .syx file in the folder of the external is read for CZ tones (CZ-101 \, 1000 \, 3000 \, 5000 with 128 bytes \, CZ-1 with 144) and they join the factory bank in alphabetical order of the files. Casio's own tones are not part of this project: put your own dumps there. \; cz4user-bank.syx in the same folder is the user bank: 64 CZ-1 tones as a librarian keeps them \, so other CZ tools read it as well. cz4user-op.syx holds the operation memory: a message of its own per used slot (F0 7D \, the ID for non-commercial use)., f 64;
#X obj 60 6618 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty All\ controls\ and\ their\ CC\ numbers 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 6646 dcw -64..63 \, CC 20: brighter or darker: added to the DCW of \;   both lines \; attack -64..63 \, CC 21: faster (-) or slower (+) steps up to \;   the sustain point of every envelope \; release -64..63 \, CC 22: faster (-) or slower (+) steps after \;   the sustain point \; balance -64..63 \, CC 23: line 1 (-) against line 2 (+) \; detune -64..63 \, CC 24: line 2 against line 1 \, in cents \, on top \;   of the tone \; vibrato 0..99 \, CC 25: extra vibrato depth \, as the mod wheel \; chorus 0..127 \, CC 26: level of the chorus for tones with \;   chorus on \; volume 0..127 \, CC 27: master volume \; line 0..1 \, CC 28: the line that the line and envelope controls \;   edit \; linesel 0..3 \, CC 29: line 1 \, line 2 \, line 1 twice (line 2 \;   detuned) \, both lines \; wave 0..7 \, CC 30: first wave of the line \; wave2 0..8 \, CC 31: second wave: the line alternates the two \;   every cycle \; window 0..7 \, CC 33: window of the resonance waves (CZ waves 6 \, \;   7 \, 8 = saw \, tri \, trap) \; ringmod 0..2 \, CC 34: line 2 ring-modulated by line 1 \, or its \;   pitch by noise (1+1' and 1+2') \; octave -1..1 \, CC 35: octave of the tone \; level 1..15 \, CC 36: level of the line (CZ-1) \; dsign 0..1 \, CC 37: detune of line 2 up or down \; doct 0..3 \, CC 39: detune of line 2 in octaves \; dnote 0..11 \, CC 40: detune of line 2 in semitones \; dfine 0..60 \, CC 41: fine detune of line 2 \, 60 = one semitone \; vwave 0..3 \, CC 42: vibrato wave \; vdelay 0..99 \, CC 43: time until the vibrato sets in \; vrate 0..99 \, CC 44: vibrato speed \; vdepth 0..99 \, CC 45: vibrato depth \; env 0..2 \, CC 46: the envelope that the rate \, level \, sus and \;   end controls edit: pitch \, wave \, amplitude \; sus 0..8 \, CC 47: step that holds while the key is down \, the \;   steps after it are the release \; end 1..8 \, CC 48: last step: it goes to zero \; kfw 0..9 \, CC 49: key follow of the DCW: high notes get less \; kfa 0..9 \, CC 50: key follow of the DCA: high notes get faster \; velp 0..15 \, CC 51: velocity to the DCO envelope (CZ-1) \; velw 0..15 \, CC 52: velocity to the DCW envelope (CZ-1) \; vela 0..15 \, CC 53: velocity to the amplitude (CZ-1) \; r1 0..99 \, CC 54: rate of step 1: 99 fastest \; r2 0..99 \, CC 55: rate of step 2: 99 fastest \; r3 0..99 \, CC 56: rate of step 3: 99 fastest \; r4 0..99 \, CC 57: rate of step 4: 99 fastest \; r5 0..99 \, CC 58: rate of step 5: 99 fastest \; r6 0..99 \, CC 59: rate of step 6: 99 fastest \; r7 0..99 \, CC 60: rate of step 7: 99 fastest \; r8 0..99 \, CC 61: rate of step 8: 99 fastest \; l1 0..99 \, CC 62: level of step 1 \; l2 0..99 \, CC 63: level of step 2 \; l3 0..99 \, CC 70: level of step 3 \; l4 0..99 \, CC 71: level of step 4 \; l5 0..99 \, CC 72: level of step 5 \; l6 0..99 \, CC 73: level of step 6 \; l7 0..99 \, CC 74: level of step 7 \; l8 0..99 \, CC 75: level of step 8 \; eattack 0..99 \, CC 76: easy envelope: attack time. Writes steps \;   1-3 of the selected envelope \; edecay 0..99 \, CC 77: easy envelope: decay time \; esustain 0..99 \, CC 78: easy envelope: sustain level \; erelease 0..99 \, CC 79: easy envelope: release time \; edit 0..1 \, CC 80: the tone that the edit controls work on: A \, \;   or B of a split or mix \; wheel 0..99 \, CC 81: vibrato depth of the mod wheel \; atvib 0..99 \, CC 82: aftertouch to vibrato depth \; atamp 0..15 \, CC 83: aftertouch to amplitude \; keymode 0..2 \, CC 85: tone A alone \, A above and B below the \;   split point \, or A and B on every key \; split 0..127 \, CC 86: split point: the lowest key of tone A \; bsrc 0..1 \, CC 87: bank of tone B \; bnum 0..127 \, CC 89: tone B: its number in that bank \; avol 0..99 \, CC 90: volume of tone A \; bvol 0..99 \, CC 91: volume of tone B \; boct -2..2 \, CC 92: octave of tone B \; bdet -64..63 \, CC 93: detune of tone B in cents (mix) \; achorus 0..1 \, CC 94: chorus for tone A \; bchorus 0..1 \, CC 95: chorus for tone B \; porta 0..1 \, CC 102: notes slide from the last one \; ptime 0..99 \, CC 103: portamento time \; glide 0..1 \, CC 104: every note starts at gnote and slides in \; gnote -24..24 \, CC 105: start of the glide \, in semitones from \;   the key \; gtime 0..99 \, CC 106: glide time \; solo 0..1 \, CC 107: one voice \, the last key. Legato keeps the \;   envelopes \; bendrange 0..12 \, CC 108: pitch bend range in semitones \; voices 1..16 \, CC 109: notes of a one-line tone (the CZ: 8) \, a \;   two-line tone plays half as many \; tune -64..63 \, CC 110: master tune in cents \; transpose -24..24 \, CC 111: transposition in semitones \; chip 0..1 \, CC 112: chip: the waves as the CZ's chip computes \;   them (12-bit) \, clean: ideal, f 64;
